course: dictionary
lesson: 2016
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around a word, its context, tell you which meaning the writer wants. The word conductor is a good example.
explain: «Metals such as copper, iron and aluminium are good conductors.» Here the words heat and electricity are clues. A conductor is a material that lets heat or electricity pass through it easily, like metal.
explain: «The conductor walked on, and the noise stopped.» Before that, the sentence describes an orchestra tuning up, so the clues point to a person who leads the music. Check by swapping your meaning in: a material walking on does not make sense, but a person does.
fact: A conductor can be a material, such as metal, that lets heat or electricity pass through it easily.
fact: An insulator is a material that does not let heat or electricity pass through easily, such as plastic, wood or rubber.
fact: A conductor can also be a person who stands in front of an orchestra, band or choir and directs the music with hand movements or a baton.
fact: On a bus or train, a conductor is the person who checks or sells tickets.
fact: A lightning conductor is a metal rod on a tall building that carries lightning safely into the ground.
exercise: «Metals such as copper, iron and aluminium are good conductors.» What does conductor mean here? | *A material that lets heat or electricity pass through it easily | A person who leads an orchestra with a baton | A person who checks tickets on a bus | A soft material that stops heat getting through
exercise: «The conductor walked on, and the noise stopped.» Who is the conductor in this sentence? | A material that lets electricity through | *The person who leads the music of an orchestra, band or choir | A metal rod on a tall building | Someone who sells tickets on a train
exercise: Pans have metal bases and plastic handles. A lightning conductor is a metal rod on a tall building. Why is it made of metal? | Metal is soft and bends easily | *Metal is a good conductor, so lightning can pass down it safely | Metal stops electricity getting in | Metal is cheaper than wood
test: Which of these is a poor conductor of heat? | Copper | *Wood | Aluminium | Iron
test: The bus conductor checked everyone's ticket before the bus left. What is a bus conductor's job? | To carry lightning into the ground | To stop heat passing through | *To check or sell tickets | To lead the music
exam: «Heat moves easily through some materials, called conductors of heat, such as metals.» What does conductor mean here? | A tall metal rod on a building | A person who sells tickets on a train | A person who leads an orchestra | *A material that lets heat move through it easily
